rts":[{"text":"செழிய","lemma":"செழிய","gloss":"O Sezhiyan!"}],"gloss":"O Sezhiyan!","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"இகழாது","parts":[{"text":"இகழ்","lemma":"இகழ்","gloss":"disregard"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ஆது","gloss":"negative suffix"}],"gloss":"without disregarding"},{"surface":"வல்லே","parts":[{"text":"வல்","lemma":"வல்","gloss":"quick"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"quickly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நிலன்","parts":[{"text":"நிலன்","lemma":"நிலன்","gloss":"land"}],"gloss":"land"},{"surface":"நெளி","parts":[{"text":"நெளி","lemma":"நெளி","gloss":"depression/low-lying"}],"gloss":"low-lying"},{"surface":"மருங்கின்","parts":[{"text":"மருங்கு","lemma":"மருங்கு","gloss":"place/side"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"locative case suffix"}],"gloss":"in the places"},{"surface":"நீர்நிலை","parts":[{"text":"நீர்","lemma":"நீர்","gloss":"water"},{"text":"நிலை","lemma":"நிலை","gloss":"reservoir/state"}],"gloss":"water reservoirs"},{"surface":"பெருக","parts":[{"text":"பெருகு","lemma":"பெருகு","gloss":"increase"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"அ","gloss":"infinitive suffix"}],"gloss":"to increase"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தட்டோர்","parts":[{"text":"தட்டோர்","lemma":"தட்டோர்","gloss":"those who built dams"}],"gloss":"those who built dams","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"அம்ம","parts":[{"text":"அம்ம","lemma":"அம்ம","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"இவண்","parts":[{"text":"இவண்","lemma":"இவண்","gloss":"here"}],"gloss":"here"},{"surface":"தட்டோரே","parts":[{"text":"தட்டோரே","lemma":"தட்டோரே","gloss":"are indeed those who established fame"}],"gloss":"are indeed those who established fame","split_unverified":true}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தள்ளாதோர்","parts":[{"text":"தள்ளு","lemma":"தள்ளு","gloss":"fail/push aside"},{"text":"ஆதோர்","lemma":"ஆதோர்","gloss":"those who did not"}],"gloss":"those who failed to do so"},{"surface":"இவண்","parts":[{"text":"இவண்","lemma":"இவண்","gloss":"here"}],"gloss":"here"},{"surface":"தள்ளாதோரே","parts":[{"text":"தள்ளு","lemma":"தள்ளு","gloss":"fail/push aside"},{"text":"ஆதோர்","lemma":"ஆதோர்","gloss":"those who did not"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"are indeed those who failed to establish anything"}]}],"literal":"Surrounding the entire roaring ocean-bound / wide world that is spread out, / bringing it by their effort and establishing their fame, / the descendants of those unique strong ancestors, / may your lifetime be as great as ten million multiplied by ten! / Where the low-hanging short Kanjira trees in the water / have their flowers bitten by groups of Vaalai fish, / and where small Aral fish and fat Varal fish / and bright-colored catfish swim in the deep moat, / which has well-shaped tall walls that make the sky fear, / O strong King of the fertile ancient town! / If you desire the wealth of the world you go to after death, / or if you desire to destroy the shoulder-strength of the world's protectors / and become the sole ruler, or if you desire / to establish excellent good fame, then / listen to the way to achieve it, O powerful one! / For all bodies which cannot exist without water, / those who gave food are those who gave life. / Food is the primary need of the body made of food. / That which is called food is land combined with water. / Those who have joined water and land here / are indeed those who created body and life in this world. / Sowing seeds and looking at the sky, even if a wide dry land / is a vast region, it will not help the effort / of the king who closely rules it. Therefore, / O Sezhiyan of conquering war, do not disregard this, and quickly / in the low-lying places of the land, make water reservoirs increase! / Those who built dams here are indeed those who established their fame; / those who failed to do so are indeed those who failed to establish anything.","translation":"May your lifetime be as long as ten million multiplied by ten, O descendant of those unique, mighty ancestors who conquered and ruled this wide world surrounded by the roaring ocean, establishing their everlasting fame! O strong King of the fertile ancient city, which has a deep moat filled with bright catfish, small eel-like Aral fish, fat Varal fish, and Vaalai fish that bite the low-hanging flowers of the Kanjira trees, and tall, well-carved walls that make the sky tremble! If you desire the bliss of the next world, or if you wish to crush the strength of other kings and become the sole ruler of this earth, or if you wish to establish enduring, glorious fame, listen to the way to achieve it, O powerful ruler! Since no body can exist without water, those who give food are the ones who give life. Food is the basis of this physical body, and food is nothing but land joined with water. Therefore, those who bring water and land together in this world are the true creators of body and life. Even if a king rules over a vast territory, if it is dry land where people sow seeds and look up to the sky for rain, it will not aid his efforts. Therefore, O Sezhiyan of conquering battles, do not disregard this advice! Quickly build reservoirs to harvest water in the low-lying areas of your land. Those who harness water here are those who secure their fame in this world; those who fail to do so will leave nothing behind.","modern":"ஒலிக்கும் கடலால் சூழப்பட்ட அகன்ற உலகத்தை வென்று, தம் புகழை நிலைநிறுத்திய வலிமைமிக்க முன்னோர்களின் வழித்தோன்றலே! நீர் சூழ்ந்த காஞ்சி மரத்தின் மலர்களைக் கவ்வும் வாளை மீன்களும், சிறிய ஆரல் மீன்களும், பருத்த வரால் மீன்களும், ஒளிரும் கெளிறு மீன்களும் நிறைந்த ஆழமான அகழியையும், வானை முட்டும் உயர்ந்த மதிலையும் கொண்ட வளமான பழமையான நகரின் வலிமைமிக்க வேந்தனே! நீ மறுமை உலகத்தின் இன்பத்தை விரும்பினாலும், பிற மன்னர்களின் தோள்வலியை அழித்து உலகிற்கு ஒருவனாய் விளங்க விரும்பினாலும், அல்லது உனது நல்ல புகழை நிலைநிறுத்த விரும்பினாலும், அதற்குரிய வழியைக் கேட்பாயாக! நீர் இல்லாமல் அமையாத உடம்புகளுக்கெல்லாம் உணவு கொடுத்தவர்களே உயிர் கொடுத்தவர்கள் ஆவர். உடம்பு உணவினால் ஆனது; உணவு என்பது நிலமும் நீரும் இணைந்ததே ஆகும். எனவே, நிலத்தையும் நீரையும் ஒன்று சேர்த்தவர்களே இவ்வுலகில் உடலையும் உயிரையும் படைத்தவர்கள் ஆவர். விதை விதைத்து மழையை எதிர்நோக்கி இருக்கும் பரந்த புன்புல நிலம் எவ்வளவு பெரியதாக இருந்தாலும், அது ஆளும் அரசனின் முயற்சிக்கு உதவாது. அதனால், போரில் வெல்லும் செழியனே! அலட்சியம் செய்யாமல், நிலத்தின் பள்ளமான பகுதிகளில் நீர்நிலைகளைப் பெருக்குவாயாக! அவ்வாறு நீர்நிலைகளை அமைத்தவர்களே இவ்வுலகில் புகழை நிலைநிறுத்தியவர்கள் ஆவர்; செய்யாதவர்கள் புகழை இழந்து அழிவர்.","explanation":"In this poem, the poet Kuṭapulavikaṉār is advising the Pāṇṭiya king Neṭuñceḻiyaṉ. The poet offers wise counsel on how the king can achieve his three main desires: heavenly bliss after death, absolute sovereignty over other kings, and eternal fame. The poet explains that life cannot exist without water, and food is the basis of life. Food is created only when land and water are joined. Therefore, a king who builds reservoirs and dams to store water is the true creator of life and will gain eternal fame. Relying solely on rain for vast dry lands is useless for a ruler's prosperity. Key phrases include 'உண்டி கொடுத்தோர் உயிர்கொடுத்தோரே' (those who gave food gave life) and 'நீர்நிலை பெருக' (to increase water reservoirs).","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.9],[0.9,1.1],[1.1,1.6],[1.6,2.3],[2.3,2.7],[2.7,2.8],[2.8,3.1],[3.1,4.4],[4.4,4.6],[4.6,4.8],[4.8,5.5],[5.5,6.22],[6.24,6.3],[6.3,7.1],[7.1,7.2],[7.2,8.5],[8.5,8.9],[8.9,9.56],[9.56,9.8],[9.8,10.2],[10.2,10.6],[10.6,10.8],[10.8,10.9],[10.9,11.6],[11.6,12.5],[12.5,12.7],[12.7,13.2],[13.2,13.5],[13.5,13.9],[13.9,14.2],[14.3,14.4],[14.4,14.7],[15.4,15.8],[15.95,16.1],[16.1,16.4],[16.4,16.8],[16.8,17.28],[17.28,17.57],[17.6,18.0],[18.0,18.3],[18.3,18.69],[18.95,19.6],[19.6,20.0],[20.0,20.5],[20.5,21.5],[21.5,21.6],[21.6,22.0],[22.0,22.4],[22.4,23.4],[23.4,23.8],[23.8,24.1],[24.1,24.4],[24.4,25.8],[25.8,26.0],[26.0,26.3],[26.3,26.7],[26.7,27.5],[27.5,27.8],[27.8,28.3],[28.3,28.8],[28.8,29.8],[29.8,30.2],[30.2,30.5],[30.5,30.6],[31.68,32.28],